- Category order.

Allow users to create, edit, reorder, and delete category cards.

Do not hardcode Greek mythology or individual deities into the application's data model. The current Greek mythology implementation is a sample configuration, not a permanent limitation.

### G. Buying Guide

Use the existing buying-guide design.

Support an editable introduction and configurable content pillars or blocks, each with its own heading, body copy, and contextual links.

The number of blocks should be configurable rather than permanently limited to three.

### H. FAQs

Use the existing visible FAQ grid.

Allow the user to add, edit, reorder, and remove questions and answers. Support inline links where appropriate.

The reference has eight FAQs, but other guides may have different numbers.

Maintain one canonical FAQ data set for each guide. The HTML renderer and schema generator must use the same saved questions and answers.

### Section management

Provide a clear section navigator.

Users must be able to:

- Add sections.
- Rename sections.
- Duplicate sections.
- Reorder sections.
- Enable or disable sections.
